MID_LGV_1_M10_Kai_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Kai_m01_001: Dad doesn't have much time left now...
MID_LGV_1_M10_Kai_m01_002: I can't get all gloomy though. I have to do everything\nI can for him and Mom.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Kai_m01: <BLN>There's no time...
MID_LGV_1_M10_Kai_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Kai_m02_001: Dad, Mom... I'm sorry... But, I can't give up.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Kai_m02: <BLN>I can't give up...
MID_LGV_1_M10_Bel_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Bel_m01_001: My soul has felt much more tranquil since last\nmonth's match.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Bel_m01_002: The hesitation, the madness—they're gone. Giving\nme strength to break through any barrier.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Bel_m01: <BLN>I will not be stopped.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Dit_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Dit_m01_001: It is always warm here in Dagda. My sister, Elfrida,\nwould appreciate this.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Dit_m01_002: On cold days she shivers. She chases the sun.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Dit_m01_003: I have told her time and again that if she were to\ntrain, she would be warm. She rejects the idea.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Dit_m01: <BLN>Yes, I think she would.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Tal_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Tal_m01_001: What? Wondering why I'm still here, are you?\nUnderstandable...
MID_LGV_1_M10_Tal_m01_002: I suppose wherever Vandahl's chief executive goes,\ncuriosity is sure to follow.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Tal_m01_003: But as for the reason I'm here, well, that's a secret!\nHaha! Anyway, good luck in the games, friend.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Tal_m01: <BLN>My reasons are...
MID_LGV_1_M10_Orh_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Orh_m01_001: Now that I've had a chance to fight in the Heroic\nGames, I've realized something.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Orh_m01_002: When I'm in battle, really giving it my all, I wind up\ngetting covered in grit and dirt!
MID_LGV_1_M10_Orh_m01_003: I suppose there's nothing to do about it, except\nsetting aside some time to wash up.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Orh_m01_004: <NCA>Tell her it's all part of battling.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Orh_m01_005: <NCB>Suggest that fighting better is cleaner.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Orh_m01_006: <ACA>I see... If that's true, I guess I'll stay focused for\nbattles in the arena...and battles with laundry!
MID_LGV_1_M10_Orh_m01_007: <ACB>Is that so? Well, good to hear. I'll train more with\nDiego then!
MID_LGA_1_M10_Orh_m01: <BLN>How unexpected!
MID_LGV_1_M10_Seo_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Seo_m01_001: The past kings of Saramis have each been marked by\ntheir own brilliant achievements.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Seo_m01_002: Delivering the people from famine... Driving off an\ninvasion by sea...
MID_LGV_1_M10_Seo_m01_003: While I am proud to follow in their worthy footsteps,\nI must carve out my own distinction among them.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Seo_m01: <BLN>The past kings of Saramis...
MID_LGV_1_M10_Led_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Led_m01_001: Don't you love a good bath? They wash so much\naway—the muck, the blood.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Led_m01_002: Not the stains of sin...but then, nothing does. And I\nwouldn't want to lose sight of those anyway.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Led_m01: <BLN>A good bath!
MID_LGV_1_M10_Anh_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Anh_m01_001: I never imagined how many experiences I'd have or\npeople I'd meet after leaving the village.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Anh_m01_002: It's a vast world and it seems intent on being harsh,\nno matter what good you are trying to accomplish.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Anh_m01_003: I push against that harshness because I have no\nchoice to do otherwise.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Anh_m01: <BLN>I never imagined...
MID_LGV_1_M10_Tia_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Tia_m01_001: I'll be Cai's friend forever.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Tia_m01_002: I decided that the first day I lived in the village. I felt\nso out of place, but Cai came to make friends.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Tia_m01_003: Whatever else happens in life, I know we'll always\nstay friends.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Tia_m01: <BLN>No matter what...
MID_LGV_1_M10_Pet_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Pet_m01_001: I'm really worried about Cai's dad.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Pet_m01_002: Him and my mom have been good friends for ages.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Pet_m01: <BLN>I'm really worried...
MID_LGV_1_M10_Hur_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Hur_m01_001: I know my main job is taking care of Aurora, not\ngoing on patrols, but...
MID_LGV_1_M10_Hur_m01_002: Sometimes I check in on a friend's grandma, or\nsomeone I know who is having a rough time.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Hur_m01_003: So, I go around and see how they're doing, and I end\nup being late for work.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Hur_m01_004: <NCA>Tell her that's priestly of her too.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Hur_m01_005: <NCB>Say it's important to watch over others.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Hur_m01_006: <ACA>It's nice to hear you say that. Almost like you've\nabsolved me of my sins, haha.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Hur_m01_007: <ACA>It's nice to hear you say that. Almost like you've\nabsolved me of my sins, haha.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Hur_m01_008: <ACB>Hmm, yeah, I suppose you're right. But it's important\nnot to interfere too much.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Hur_m01_009: <ACB>Hmm, yes, you're right. But it's also important\nnot to interfere too much...
MID_LGA_1_M10_Hur_m01: <BLN>I know my main job...
MID_LGV_1_M10_Max_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Max_m01_001: Gah! Wouldn't you know? Looks like I frayed\nmy sleeve.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Max_m01_002: A gladiator shouldn't show up to his audience\nlooking shabby.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Max_m01_003: I'll stitch that up. Can't be a clown if you don't\nhave nimble fingers, heh heh.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Max_m01: <BLN>Part of the job!
MID_LGV_1_M10_Gol_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Gol_m01_001: You seen those red marks on my big brother's body?\nThey look like godmarks. They're COOL!
MID_LGV_1_M10_Gol_m01_002: I've also got tattoos on my body, but they're the ones\nmy tribe gave me.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Gol_m01_003: It's waaay cooler having your own special ones!\nThink I should get some of those?
MID_LGA_1_M10_Gol_m01: <BLN>Look at his tattoos!
MID_LGV_1_M10_Gat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Gat_m01_001: As we watch the varied ways warriors fight in the\nHeroic Games, I ask... What makes a gladiator?
MID_LGV_1_M10_Gat_m01_002: To me, it is harmony between mind and body and\ntechnique. Beautiful, beastly balance.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Gat_m01_003: I train daily in hopes of meeting that ideal.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Gat_m01_004: <NCA>Say he's got a ways to go.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Gat_m01_005: <NCB>Say he's too refined to be "beastly."
MID_LGV_1_M10_Gat_m01_006: <ACA>Aha, yes, indeed. There's much training for me to\ndo yet.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Gat_m01_007: <ACA>Aha, yes, exactly so. There is much training for me to\ndo yet.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Gat_m01_008: <ACB>You're saying I lack what it takes to be a gladiator?\nWell—you're wrong.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Gat_m01_009: <ACB>You mean to suggest I lack what it takes to be a\ngladiator? Well—I disagree.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Gat_m01: <BLN>What makes a gladiator?
MID_LGV_1_M10_Dan_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Dan_m01_001: The people fill Dagsion to the brim, and business\nis booming—transcription houses' included!
MID_LGV_1_M10_Dan_m01_002: Naturally, the heart of the continent is home to some\nof its finest scribes. That said, if what I hear is true...
MID_LGV_1_M10_Dan_m01_003: some customers are less interested in reading our\nbooks than decorating shelves with them.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Dan_m01: <BLN>Transcription houses are booming!
MID_LGV_1_M10_Fab_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Fab_m01_001: There are many in this land who conceal their\nidentities. It is worrisome.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Fab_m01_002: I have no interest in these beasts, but unpredictable\nelements could throw my plans askew.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Fab_m01_003: Someone simple and manageable like Esmeralda\nis preferable.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Fab_m01: <BLN>It is worrisome.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Esm_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Esm_m01_001: The people of Saramis are interesting! They're called\na "forest people," but they're also good with boats.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Esm_m01_002: A little while ago I got to sit and chat about seafaring\nwith them. I had a great time!
MID_LGV_1_M10_Esm_m01_003: So many people seem to hate Saramis, but we're all\nthe same. They just need to get to know them.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Esm_m01: <BLN>The people of Saramis...
MID_LGV_1_M10_Urs_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Urs_m01_001: You're a winner, through and through. No wonder\nTalimun has his eye on you.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Urs_m01_002: He might know what to say to make others FEEL\nclose, but it doesn't mean he considers them as such.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Urs_m01_003: Because to him, he's always number one. So, know\nthat a genuine interest is rare...
MID_LGV_1_M10_Urs_m01_004: <NCA>Tell her you're honored.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Urs_m01_005: <NCB>Tell her you've noticed his eyes on her as well.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Urs_m01_006: <ACA>Is that so? I'm sure he'll be delighted to hear it.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Urs_m01_007: <ACB>Hm, I wonder... I simply stand by his side.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Urs_m01: <BLN>He has his eye on you.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Sim_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Sim_m01_001: There's a strange little group making moves behind\nthis tournament, so Talimun asked me to stay alert.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Sim_m01_002: To be honest, I don't really care what they're up to\nas long as I get to smash them in the end.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Sim_m01_003: After all, I'm not some detective or politician.\nI'm an axe, plain and simple.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Sim_m01: <BLN>Let them try something...
MID_LGV_1_M10_Lou_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Lou_m01_001: The Heroic Games... It all went by so fast.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Lou_m01_002: You know, out of all that's happened, the baths were\nprobably my favorite part.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Lou_m01_003: Once I leave, I may not be able to come back for a\nwhile, so I should enjoy them while I can!
MID_LGA_1_M10_Lou_m01: <BLN>My favorite part was...
MID_LGV_1_M10_Fia_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Fia_m01_001: I found the most wonderful restaurant the other day!\nThey had so many surprisingly spicy foods.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Fia_m01_002: The shop owner seemed a little timid, but he had\nlots of things to try.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Fia_m01_003: There weren't many people in there either. Ahhh, it\nwas like a dream!
MID_LGA_1_M10_Fia_m01: <BLN>I loved it.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Die_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Die_m01_001: Orchel is very powerful, when you consider her\nmagic, strength, and ability to purify.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Die_m01_002: But she is too kind for her own good, which is\nwhy I task myself with her protection.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Die_m01: <BLN>Orchel is very powerful, but...
MID_LGV_1_M10_Lor_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Lor_m01_001: My back used to ache when I'd soak in water...\nFunny though. It's not hurting these days.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Lor_m01_002: Seems like it's healed up fully since all that\ntime ago, but I've still got some scars.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Lor_m01_003: I used to live a rougher life—and got punished for it.\nBut everything changed for me a while ago.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Lor_m01: <BLN>Wait a minute...
MID_LGV_1_M10_Set_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Set_m01_001: Do you possess a clear sense of your purpose?\nAh, forgive me. I've just been thinking.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Set_m01_002: One should try to improve one's own standing in\nlife, of course, whatever their means.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Set_m01_003: But I'd also warn against doing so at the expense\nof others. A complete perspective is essential.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Set_m01: <BLN>Remain mindful.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Nin_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Nin_m01_001: The vulkans in Credna's temple are so capable,\ngathering weapons, gleaning details on enemies.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Nin_m01_002: They often suggest that I should rest more. And so\nI do rest more. I'm thankful for their concern.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Nin_m01: <BLN>The vulkans in Credna's temple...
MID_LGV_1_M10_Bon_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Bon_m01_001: Dagda is divided into 46 counties, of which four are\nwithin Saraminian territory.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Bon_m01_002: But the empire still collects tithes from all counties,\nincluding those in Arago and Brezarant.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Bon_m01_003: Complete independence from the temples may prove\na difficult goal for our people to reach...
MID_LGA_1_M10_Bon_m01: <BLN>It is a thorny problem.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Tob_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Tob_m01_001: The boss has really come into her own, both as a\nwarrior and a queen.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Tob_m01_002: But she can't do it all alone. She's still young...\nor maybe brash is a better word.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Tob_m01_003: That arm probably makes her think she's stronger\nthan she is. Good thing she's got me and Bona!
MID_LGA_1_M10_Tob_m01: <BLN>The boss has grown up fast.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Lil_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Lil_m01_001: No matter how many corners you cut elsewhere,\nyou gotta eat right.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Lil_m01_002: My father always told me not to neglect my archery\ntraining or my meals.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Lil_m01_003: Hunting with a bow gets me both practice and food,\nso it's like killing two birds with one shot.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Lil_m01: <BLN>It takes care of two things at once.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Lys_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Lys_m01_001: If only I had a brain like Commander Bonaventure's,\ncapable of remembering the smallest detail.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Lys_m01_002: But it's pointless to ask for things I'll never have.\nI should ask instead what I can do with my skills.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Lys_m01: <BLN>I should trust in my own strengths.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Buc_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Buc_m01_001: I hear Poloni belongs to the bureau of construction,\nbut he hardly seems suited for the role.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Buc_m01_002: When Lord Guillermo was a praetor, those appointed\nto such offices were highly competent.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Buc_m01_003: Day and night, he would debate with the other\npraetors or Father Mahdel... A different time.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Buc_m01: <BLN>That man, Poloni...
MID_LGV_1_M10_Sci_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Sci_m01_001: In addition to the arts, Kalla is also the goddess of\nhunting. She often takes up her bow to pursue prey.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Sci_m01_002: And the lovely smile she has on her face when she\ndoes it! Nothing is more beautiful.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Sci_m01: <BLN>Ah, that smile!
MID_LGV_1_M10_Moo_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Moo_m01_001: I think I've been drinking too much coffee. I can\nhardly sleep.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Moo_m01_002: It's just so much fun to make! I even carved my own\nequipment out of wood.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Moo_m01_003: Then I mix in medicinal herbs to change up\nthe taste...but I should probably cut back.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Moo_m01: <BLN>Maybe I've had too much?
MID_LGV_1_M10_Mic_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Mic_m01_001: It's strange... Fabio seems almost happy lately. His\nmuttering even sounds upbeat.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Mic_m01_002: Something good must have happened, but he still\nmust give such a creepy impression to others.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Mic_m01: <BLN>Something must have happened.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Oly_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Oly_m01_001: I am racked with indecision! What emotion should\nI try to express in this song?
MID_LGV_1_M10_Oly_m01_002: A friend of mine asked me to perform at her\nwedding, you see.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Oly_m01_003: The marriage was arranged by her parents—and she\nherself does not want it! How can I celebrate that?
MID_LGV_1_M10_Oly_m01_004: <NCA>Tell her to stop thinking and sing.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Oly_m01_005: <NCB>Tell her to feign being celebratory.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Oly_m01_006: <ACA>You mean to say that I ought to simply sing,\nwithout a care in the world?
MID_LGV_1_M10_Oly_m01_007: <ACA>Certainly, that would be more sincere toward my\nfriend, and toward my art, rather than feigning joy.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Oly_m01_008: <ACA>You mean to say that I must simply sing, without a\ncare in the world?
MID_LGV_1_M10_Oly_m01_009: <ACA>Certainly, that would be more sincere toward my\nfriend, and toward my art, rather than feigning joy.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Oly_m01_010: <ACB>But if I did that, it would not be meaningful!
MID_LGV_1_M10_Oly_m01_011: <ACB>Perhaps so...but if I did that, would it really be\nmeaningful?
MID_LGA_1_M10_Oly_m01: <BLN>What to do!
MID_LGV_1_M10_Naz_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Naz_m01_001: It's fun to do barehanded martial arts, but swinging\nweapons around is fun too. Really clears my mind!
MID_LGV_1_M10_Naz_m01_002: If you keep swinging, it starts to feel like you and\nyour weapon become one.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Naz_m01_003: That's why I try everything in life. I'd hate to be good\nat something, but never know because I didn't try!
MID_LGA_1_M10_Naz_m01: <BLN>You gotta try!
MID_LGV_1_M10_Sar_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Sar_m01_001: Anatolia...
MID_LGV_1_M10_Sar_m01_002: I've got to do whatever I can too. For the sakes of\neveryone in the village.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Sar_m01: <BLN>Anatolia...
MID_LGV_1_M10_Sar_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Sar_m02_001: For now, I've been able to sort things out.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Sar_m02_002: Luckily, I can contact Anatolia through Jiang.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Sar_m02_003: I'm going to stay put a little longer so I can keep\ngathering information.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Sar_m02: <BLN>For now...
MID_LGV_1_M10_Dai_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Dai_m01_001: Even in a city as prosperous as Dagsion, there's still\npeople who can't get food.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Dai_m01_002: Since kids aren't strong enough to hunt, I shared\na bit of meat with them.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Dai_m01_003: I can't take 'em with me, but I'd like to come back\nhere from time to time to check in on 'em.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Dai_m01: <BLN>I worry about 'em.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Hal_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Hal_m01_001: Did you know some tricks can be dangerous if you\nmess them up? I was scared of that at first...
MID_LGV_1_M10_Hal_m01_002: But, as I did them over and over, I got better at them.\nPretty soon, I wasn't scared anymore.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Hal_m01_003: Best part is that I really enjoy the time that I spend\npracticing. Being focused like that suits me.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Hal_m01: <BLN>Practicing tricks keeps you safe...
MID_LGV_1_M10_Guj_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Guj_m01_001: Want to know how I've survived so many battles?\nI don't worry about winning each and every time.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Guj_m01_002: There are always more battles to come, so always\nbet on your future.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Guj_m01_003: Well, I don't mind it when people fight with all their\nmight around me though. Admirable!
MID_LGA_1_M10_Guj_m01: <BLN>A survival tip!
MID_LGV_1_M10_Yan_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Yan_m01_001: Yu Phas helped our ancestors, but I cannot forgive\nher for urging us to abandon the written word.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Yan_m01_002: That is nothing less than purging ourselves of all\nthe words and knowledge we'd inherited.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Yan_m01_003: Most of all, did they not think it a waste to lose\nthat evocative, powerful ancient writing?!
MID_LGA_1_M10_Yan_m01: <BLN>Unforgivable!
MID_LGV_1_M10_Iio_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Iio_m01_001: I've had time to ponder what exactly makes a\nknight...a knight.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Iio_m01_002: I've started to realize that I wasn't giving training\nmy all—that I'm drifting from my ideals.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Iio_m01_003: What I must do to correct this is put distraction\naside and train with pure purpose.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Iio_m01: <BLN>I've been pondering...
MID_LGV_1_M10_Pep_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Pep_m01_001: We like to buy sweets for the little ones who have\npresented us with much help.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Pep_m01_002: Ha! We have learned, for instance, how to conduct\nourselves in the market.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Pep_m01_003: Oh, those rascals in their shops who've called us\nthe "kid who stinks at shopping" will rue the day!
MID_LGV_1_M10_Pep_m01_004: But it's the haggling that makes us uneasy. Is it not\nmore dignified to set and pay an established price?
MID_LGA_1_M10_Pep_m01: <BLN>Ha! We are learning!
MID_LGV_1_M10_Noc_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Noc_m01_001: If I won the Heroic Games, I would wish to keep\nliving in Dagsion forever.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Noc_m01_002: Living the city life I've always dreamed of...living a\nlife of leisure... Oh, how wonderful.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Noc_m01_003: I wonder what the final winner of the games will\nwish for?
MID_LGA_1_M10_Noc_m01: <BLN>If I won the games...
MID_LGV_1_M10_Sop_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Sop_m01_001: May the world be sweet and savory...
MID_LGV_1_M10_Sop_m01_002: May someone invent a seasoning that turns the\nundelicious...delicious!
MID_LGV_1_M10_Sop_m01_003: May banquets appear out of thin air whenever\nI like... Well, one of those would be my wish!
MID_LGA_1_M10_Sop_m01: <BLN>My own wishes...
MID_LGV_1_M10_Cat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Cat_m01_001: I heard a strange noise in an alley and rushed in to\nfind a girl being thrashed for suspicion of theft.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Cat_m01_002: Stealing is wrong. But there's some foolishness\nin letting yourself be stolen from!
MID_LGV_1_M10_Cat_m01_003: I hauled them both before the temples for judgment.\nThe girl told me I'd saved her life.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Cat_m01_004: I didn't exactly mean it as a good deed, but I don't\nmind people thinking of it that way either.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Cat_m01: <BLN>I only did what I had to.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Ned_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Ned_m01_001: I saw two children who looked like sisters walking\nalong, eating sweets.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Ned_m01_002: It took me right back to the days I played with\nLilian when we were both little.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Ned_m01_003: Although...it wasn't sweets we were carrying, but\nsome prey we'd hunted together in the wild.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Ned_m01: <BLN>It took me right back...
MID_LGV_1_M10_Zac_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Zac_m01_001: Bah! What is it? Does he have stuff inked into\nhis skin? I've got THAT.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Zac_m01_002: Everyone's goin' on and on about how cool this\nWhite-Maned Demon is. I don't like it!
MID_LGA_1_M10_Zac_m01: <BLN>What's with people?!
MID_LGV_1_M10_Maj_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Maj_m01_001: I'm gonna get a great statue of the great Majide\nbuilt—big as the one in the plaza!
MID_LGV_1_M10_Maj_m01_002: No! Ten of 'em, all in a row!
MID_LGV_1_M10_Maj_m01_003: NO! Ten in a row, ten times that size! I'll make\nthe whole thing myself!
MID_LGA_1_M10_Maj_m01: <BLN>A statue of me!
MID_LGV_1_M10_Ven_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Ven_m01_001: Youngsters these days! No manners. The future\nof this land is descending into ruin.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Ven_m01_002: In my day, people were tough, hard-working, and\nhad manners. Generation before that, more so!
MID_LGV_1_M10_Ven_m01_003: Why does each passing age strip people of good\ncharacter?! Shameless fools, everywhere.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Ven_m01: <BLN>Shameless fools!
MID_LGV_1_M10_Ini_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Ini_m01_001: They warnt me... They warnt me long ago... Mom\nand Dad said men weren't all stand-up types.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Ini_m01_002: Ach, not like back home... Here, you never know\nwhen a bunch of no-goods are on the chase.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Ini_m01: <BLN>I was warnt...
MID_LGV_1_M10_Jas_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Jas_m01_001: I haven't got any idea who's going to win.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Jas_m01_002: I'm usually a pretty good judge of these things,\nbeing a mercenary and all.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Jas_m01_003: But when it's such an unusual matchup, there's\nno way I could make a call. Ha ha!
MID_LGA_1_M10_Jas_m01: <BLN>I can't predict it.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Ale_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Ale_m01_001: There are many in the temples who don't think well\nof me, given who my uncle is.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Ale_m01_002: But some will always see me as a knight, like my\ncomrades in the Silver Knights of Tellus.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Ale_m01_003: That I fell in with them was a true blessing in my\nlife, both for me and Bucephalus.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Ale_m01: <BLN>A true blessing.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Cen_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Cen_m01_001: I come from a long line of knights. My family has\npledged loyalty to the temples for generations. 
MID_LGV_1_M10_Cen_m01_002: Divine Sovereign Solel himself recommended\nthat I be Aurora's chief celestial general.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Cen_m01_003: I will not disgrace that honor. I perform my duty to\nmy fullest, day in, day out.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Cen_m01_004: Good grief... I'd like to make that boy write up\nthe report.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Cen_m01_005: But, this one time, in the name of my friend, I do\nbelieve everything happening is for the best.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Cen_m01: <BLN>I have my honor...
MID_LGV_1_M10_Kir_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Kir_m01_001: The name Kiroc still means something—he who\nspreads his wings in terror!
MID_LGV_1_M10_Kir_m01_002: Some young rascal looked at me and asked if\nI was Kiroc...THE Kiroc!
MID_LGV_1_M10_Kir_m01_003: That pipsqueak made my day. I said he could join\nmy Black-Swan Pirates anytime.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Kir_m01: <BLN>The name has weight!
MID_LGV_1_M10_Nuz_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Nuz_m01_001: Citizens of the capital seem to be frightened of me at\nnight, saying I "appear suddenly from the darkness."
MID_LGV_1_M10_Nuz_m01_002: I have excellent night vision and can walk through\ndarkness without a light...which is now a liability.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Nuz_m01: <BLN>Is it my fault?
MID_LGV_1_M10_Gab_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Gab_m01_001: The cost of food—ALL food—went up this year.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Gab_m01_002: Now I have to sit down with Poloni and ask him to\nbump our budget. That'll be fun.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Gab_m01: <BLN>This year...
MID_LGV_1_M10_Lin_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Lin_m01_001: What do you think of your mother?
MID_LGV_1_M10_Lin_m01_002: <NCA>Say you like her.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Lin_m01_003: <NCB>Say you dislike her.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Lin_m01_004: <ACA>I see. That is well and good. You ought to treasure\nyour mother.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Lin_m01_005: <ACB>Such disgusting disrespect. None of us would be alive\nif not for our mothers.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Lin_m01: <BLN>What do you think of your mother?
MID_LGV_1_M10_Nat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Nat_m01_001: I'm afraid I've fallen out of shape since I got here.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Nat_m01_002: Perhaps I'd better go out hunting now and again for\na change of pace.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Nat_m01_003: Maybe I'll run into a bear! That would be an\ninteresting fight.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Nat_m01: <BLN>A little out of shape.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Hri_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Hri_m01_001: I never liked the Order of the Haze—those people\nwho attend the king.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Hri_m01_002: "Private soldiers of House Amalfrida," people called\nthem. Not anymore. They're a bunch of assassins.
MID_LGA_1_M10_Hri_m01: <BLN>The Order of the Haze...
MID_LGV_1_M10_Ann_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Ann_m01_001: Guess the Heroic Games are just about over.\nI wonder who'll end up with the big prize.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Ann_m01_002: It seems like so long ago we were drawing up plans\nfor a tournament...but also like it was yesterday.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Ann_m01_003: Sorry, just got swept up in my feelings there.\nAre you gonna buy something or not?
MID_LGA_1_M10_Ann_m01: <BLN>The Heroic Games are almost over.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Ann_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Ann_m02_001: The Heroic Games are ending soon. I wonder who'll\nend up with the winner's garland.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Ann_m02_002: The whole thing took ages to prepare, and it feels\nlike it happened in a flash.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Ann_m02_003: That's a little sad...but hey, now I'll have more free\ntime to focus on my little shop.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Ann_m02_004: I told you about that, right? I run a secret shop that's\nopen by night. Come visit after sundown!
MID_LGA_1_M10_Ann_m02: <BLN>The Heroic Games are about over.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Miw_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Miw_m01_001: Growing old means I've more days behind me\nthan ahead, but...
MID_LGV_1_M10_Miw_m01_002: I'll be spending that time with my family!
MID_LGV_1_M10_Miw_m01_003: With that blessing, I know I will be able to pass from\nthis world with no regrets...
MID_LGA_1_M10_Miw_m01: <BLN>More days behind than ahead...
MID_LGV_1_M10_Cle_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Cle_m01_001: We hiked all the way out here and what do we have\nto show for it? Zilch. 
MID_LGV_1_M10_Cle_m01_002: Thales isn't going to like that one little bit.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Cle_m01_003: He'll rake us over the coals. I need to come up with\na good story. What a pain in the tushy.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Cle_m01_004: Better try and pin it on Myson.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Cle_m01_005: Why oh why did they send me? 
MID_LGA_1_M10_Cle_m01: <BLN>What a pain in the tushy.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Mys_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_Mys_m01_001: We were faced with one insurmountable problem on\nthis little trip: we're not on our home turf.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Mys_m01_002: Fact is, Cleobulus held me back too. It's not me\nwho's screwing things up, and that's for sure.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Mys_m01_003: All that said, it's high time we retreated. We need to\ntalk to Thales about next steps.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Mys_m01_004: What we should do now is head north and look for\na ship that'll take us back to Fódlan.
MID_LGV_1_M10_Mys_m01_005: I'm so tired of traveling with somebody who does\nwhatever he pleases!
MID_LGA_1_M10_Mys_m01: <BLN>Looking back...
MID_LGV_1_M10_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_B01_m01_001: My old man's gotten so excited about the main\nmatches. He's started saying he's going to enter.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B01_m01_002: "I used to be a gladiator," he says. "Some clan or\nother will take me, I'm sure!"
MID_LGV_1_M10_B01_m01_003: I had a hard time getting him to see reason. He's way\npast his prime...I wish he wouldn't be so reckless.
MID_LGA_1_M10_B01_m01: <BLN>My old man is impossible.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_B02_m01_001: The ones who made it this far aren't your ordinary\nfighters. They're all a couple steps past normal.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B02_m01_002: When that's the kind of opposition you're up against,\nthe smart thing to do is to drop out.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B02_m01_003: A mercenary who gets hurt in the games can't work,\nand there's no coming back from that.
MID_LGA_1_M10_B02_m01: <BLN>The smart thing is to drop out.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_B03_m01_001: *sigh* I'd love to goof off and watch the matches.\nBut not while our performance is being evaluated.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B03_m01_002: If I miss out on a promotion because I shirked my\njob, I'll regret it. So here I'll stay, keeping alert!
MID_LGV_1_M10_B03_m01_003: But it's torture having to do it while I can hear the\ncrowd cheering. I wanna know what happens!
MID_LGA_1_M10_B03_m01: <BLN>I want to see the matches!
MID_LGV_1_M10_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_B04_m01_001: How can everyone stand to watch this savagery?\nThe blood, the screams...what's the draw here?
MID_LGV_1_M10_B04_m01_002: I put up with it in the name of awakening Dagda the\nGreat, but I hope it's all over soon.
MID_LGA_1_M10_B04_m01: <BLN>Such savage cruelty...
MID_LGV_1_M10_B05_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_B05_m01_001: Why won't anyone believe that I fought in the\nqualifiers?
MID_LGV_1_M10_B05_m01_002: Everyone assumes I'm fibbing. I'm even starting to\nwonder if I really did make it all up...
MID_LGA_1_M10_B05_m01: <BLN>Why won't they believe me?
MID_LGV_1_M10_B06_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_B06_m01_001: The dates harvested from the orchard at Jurah's\ntemple are sent to branch temples all over the land.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B06_m01_002: From there, the temples distribute them to the\npeople. Many people eagerly await this time of year.
MID_LGA_1_M10_B06_m01: <BLN>We're truly grateful.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B07_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_B07_m01_001: Ohh, my poor knees. I don't know how I managed\nthe hike to the branch temple.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B07_m01_002: Will I have to tough it out like this for the rest of\nmy days? Ughhh, the pain...
MID_LGA_1_M10_B07_m01: <BLN>My knees...
MID_LGV_1_M10_B08_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_B08_m01_001: Making repairs on the branch temple always gets\nme so wound up.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B08_m01_002: It's delicate work, so I can't lose focus, but it's\nnerve-racking to be doing it for a god.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B08_m01_003: The silver lining is that it does make me proud to\nthink that my work will last for hundreds of years.
MID_LGA_1_M10_B08_m01: <BLN>Can't make a single mistake...
MID_LGV_1_M10_B09_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_B09_m01_001: The guy on the other side of the street really started\nlooking old after his wife left.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B09_m01_002: I don't know why. She won't be gone long—she only\nwent to see her relatives in Maybell.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B09_m01_003: Maybe he was too drunk to understand what she was\ntelling him. I think she was worried about that.
MID_LGA_1_M10_B09_m01: <BLN>Maybe I ought to tell him...
MID_LGV_1_M10_B10_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_B10_m01_001: The leaders of the clans who made it to the main\nmatches pretty much all have bloodmarks.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B10_m01_002: In other words, they're related in some way to Dagda\nthe Great. They must be excited for his revival.
MID_LGA_1_M10_B10_m01: <BLN>You know what bloodmarks mean.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B11_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_B11_m01_001: I wouldn't recommend trying to rob a mercenary,\neven one who's falling-down drunk.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B11_m01_002: They might look out of it, but I guarantee they aren't.\nIf one of them gets their hands on you, it's over.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B11_m01_003: No, the best targets are priests. They tend to carry\nlots of coin for their official business, heheh.
MID_LGA_1_M10_B11_m01: <BLN>Let me give you some advice...
MID_LGV_1_M10_B12_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_B12_m01_001: My aunt in Tellus had a fall, so my mom and I are\ngoing over there to help her out.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B12_m01_002: My big brother forced me into it, saying, "You're the\nyoungest—you go!" The pitfalls of being born last.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B12_m01_003: It's going to mean I'll be away for half the year!\nAnd I really wanted to see the finals...
MID_LGA_1_M10_B12_m01: <BLN>What a disappointment...
MID_LGV_1_M10_B13_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_B13_m01_001: My friend next door says she really loves boats.\nSo I came along to take a look!
MID_LGV_1_M10_B13_m01_002: I want to learn what's so good about them. She's my\nfriend, so I want to know more about her interests.
MID_LGA_1_M10_B13_m01: <BLN>So this is what she's into.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B14_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_B14_m01_001: The boat's gone on without me. It's so dull having to\nstay back at home.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B14_m01_002: My crewmates had to drag me off the decks, saying,\n"Don't force yourself to set sail when you're sick!"
MID_LGV_1_M10_B14_m01_003: I was trying to hide it, but they must have figured it\nout. Nothing to do now but rest up like I was told.
MID_LGA_1_M10_B14_m01: <BLN>So boring...
MID_LGV_1_M10_B15_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_B15_m01_001: I'm always a bit anxious making deliveries to\nVandahl. Any slight problems and they send it back.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B15_m01_002: On the other hand, they're enthusiastic about quality.\nI love getting to pass that back to the artisans.
MID_LGA_1_M10_B15_m01: <BLN>I'm a little anxious...
MID_LGV_1_M10_B16_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_B16_m01_001: Credna doesn't have a wife, right?
MID_LGV_1_M10_B16_m01_002: Surely there's no shortage of suitors for a god.\nSo what's taking him so long?
MID_LGA_1_M10_B16_m01: <BLN>Credna's not married...right?
MID_LGV_1_M10_B17_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_B17_m01_001: I managed to get myself a nice smoked pig. I can't\nwait to dig in!
MID_LGV_1_M10_B17_m01_002: The only seasoning I'll use is a chunk of salt. That\nway I can enjoy the natural flavors of the meat.
MID_LGA_1_M10_B17_m01: <BLN>This is going to be delicious!
MID_LGV_1_M10_B18_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_B18_m01_001: When will we be rid of all these country bumpkins?\nIt's such a nuisance having them around.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B18_m01_002: People are going to think I, a born-and-bred citizen,\nam one of these hayseeds. I can't stand it!
MID_LGA_1_M10_B18_m01: <BLN>What a nuisance...
MID_LGV_1_M10_B19_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_B19_m01_001: Nobles have such long names that they're hard to\nremember. But they're my business partners, so...
MID_LGV_1_M10_B19_m01_002: Could I maybe get around having to say them?\nNo, they'd probably notice. Ugh...
MID_LGA_1_M10_B19_m01: <BLN>It's just too much...
MID_LGV_1_M10_B20_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_B20_m01_001: The scandal of the disappearances in Aurora's temple\nhas been cleared up now.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B20_m01_002: Apparently, the true culprit was a painter who was\nfamous in his day.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B20_m01_003: I wonder if that's related to the painting of paradise\nbeing smashed to pieces.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B20_m01_004: Well, either way, I suppose Aurora will be making\npublic appearances again.
MID_LGA_1_M10_B20_m01: <BLN>Heard the good news?
MID_LGV_1_M10_B21_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_B21_m01_003: Hanging out at the tavern and arguing with the gang\nis the best part of my day.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B21_m01_004: Lately we've been fixated on who's gonna win the\nHeroic Games.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B21_m01_005: Everyone's got opinions, and it usually gets so heated\nthat it turns into a shouting match.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B21_m01_001: I hear a certain royal went on a bit of a rampage\nat Aurora's temple. I hope everything is OK.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B21_m01_002: Someone who saw it all said it was quite a scene.
MID_LGA_1_M10_B21_m01: <BLN>Heard the latest gossip?
MID_LGV_1_M10_B22_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_B22_m01_001: Word of advice. Don't go looking into flamma.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B22_m01_002: It's a surefire way to draw the attention of the\nOrder of Mithras.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B22_m01_003: That's all I feel comfortable saying.
MID_LGA_1_M10_B22_m01: <BLN>A word of advice.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B23_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_B23_m01_001: I've managed to procure a lot of rare goods, so it's\ntime I went back to Fódlan.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B23_m01_002: Hopefully I don't miss the next boat—I'm not sure\nwhen I can make it home after that.
MID_LGA_1_M10_B23_m01: <BLN>It's about time I went back.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B24_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_B24_m01_001: There isn't much clarity about the lifespans of\ndemigods.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B24_m01_002: Several individuals are recorded as having lived up\nto five hundred years.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B24_m01_003: Which reminds me—they say gods don't have\nheartbeats, but is that also true of demigods?
MID_LGA_1_M10_B24_m01: <BLN>The details are unclear...
MID_LGV_1_M10_B25_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M10_B25_m01_001: Word of advice for you.
MID_LGV_1_M10_B25_m01_002: Upstanding folks don't go looking for flamma. Sure, it\nmakes you strong, but it's better to stay off the stuff.
MID_LGA_1_M10_B25_m01: <BLN>My advice?